*.wasm
page.svg
page.png

# `go build ./cmd/x` with no -o drops the binary HERE, named after the directory.
# One entry per command, and TestNoBinaryIsTracked derives this list from cmd/ and
# fails if a new command is not covered — a line naming a binary dies at the next
# rename, which is how a 3.5MB gotex-linediff and a 5.8MB gotex were committed.
/gotex
/gotex-wasm
/gotex-abdiff
/gotex-coverage
/gotex-linediff
/gotex-refdiff

# Claude Code keeps its per-session worktrees here. They are real git
# repositories, so a "git add -A" records nineteen gitlinks in one stroke — which
# is how this line came to be written.
/.claude/

# test binaries left by `go test -cpuprofile`, which is how a 29MB engine.test
# nearly went into a commit
*.test
